00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.360
And you can design
it for one team,

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.430
and then you can
simply switch the view

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:24.866
and look at the same information
for other teams, as well.

00:09:24.866 --> 00:09:26.240
And you can do
quick comparisons.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.590
PETE FRISELLA: Sure.

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:30.390
MINHAZ KAZI: Now, we've
seen some examples

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:33.180
of the dashboards, and we'll
see later how we can build them.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:36.042
But let's talk a little
bit about Data Studio.

00:09:36.042 --> 00:09:37.500
As I mentioned
earlier, Data Studio

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:41.070
is the next-generation business
intelligence and visualization

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:42.780
tool from Google.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.170
It's completely free.

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:47.550
You can use it right now, by
going to datastudio.google.com.

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.530
The way Data Studio
works is that, first, you

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:50.850
connect to your data.

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:52.990
Then you try to
visualize your data.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.170
And then while
you're visualizing,

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.020
you can set it up either
for exploratory analysis,

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:00.650
or you can also do explanatory
where you're trying

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:01.900
to share it with other people.

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:03.480
And once that is
ready, you basically

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.230
set up your dashboard
so that other people

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.850
can view your work.

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:08.890
So let's go through
these steps one by one.

00:10:11.466 --> 00:10:13.590
When you're connecting to
your data in Data Studio,

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.190
you have lots of
options available.

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:16.398
You have a lot of connectors.

00:10:16.398 --> 00:10:19.350
You can connect to
internal Google data

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:23.160
sources, like Sheets, BigQuery,
Cloud SQL, and Cloud Storage.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.200
Your data might be
already present there,

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.397
or your data might be
outside of these sources.

00:10:27.397 --> 00:10:29.730
And you can bring in your
data from your on-premise data

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.729
source, or external source,
and bring those data

00:10:31.729 --> 00:10:33.180
into these sources.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.400
You can also bring in
your existing information

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.110
from Google Analytics,
AdWords, YouTube.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.810
We have direct connectors
available for this.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:43.200
You might also have
on-premise data in MySQL or

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.890
[? Postgres. ?] And Data
Studio can connect directly

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:49.020
to those data sources,
to those databases,

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.970
and bring the data into Data
Studio for you to analyze.

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:55.560
Now, these are mostly
Google data sources,

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:58.200
but what if your data
is somewhere else?

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.350
What if you have to access
your data using a public API?

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:02.850
Or you have on-premise
data that you

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:05.490
can access using a private API?

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.550
That's where community
connectors come in.

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:10.200
Community connectors are
connectors for Data Studio

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.600
that are designed by the
Data Studio community.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:18.030
They let you get your
data from any API--

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.760
that might include
WebAPI or JDBC--

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:24.277
and bring that data into Data
Studio for you to analyze.

00:11:24.277 --> 00:11:25.110
PETE FRISELLA: Yeah.

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:26.580
It's a very powerful feature.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.770
We've seen a lot of
people using this feature

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:31.229
to bring in data that's not
necessarily publicly available.

00:11:31.229 --> 00:11:32.978
Maybe it's something
just for your company

00:11:32.978 --> 00:11:34.437
that you might have
a specific API,

00:11:34.437 --> 00:11:36.061
and you really want
to be able to allow

00:11:36.061 --> 00:11:37.882
your users within your
company to analyze

00:11:37.882 --> 00:11:39.090
that data within Data Studio.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.864
So this really gives you a great
option to extend the platform

00:11:41.864 --> 00:11:44.280
and bring in data that's really
important to your business

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:48.240
or specifically to some use
case that you might have.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.820
And we actually have a
lot built by our partners

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:52.742
already that are
supported by our partners.

00:11:52.742 --> 00:11:54.450
But we've definitely
seen a lot of growth

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:57.390
around just companies
building their own connectors

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:59.040
to meet their use case.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:11:59.915
MINHAZ KAZI: Exactly.

00:11:59.915 --> 00:12:01.397
PETE FRISELLA: Yeah.

00:12:01.397 --> 00:12:02.980
A large number of
connectors have been

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:04.390
built, which has been great.

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.870
MINHAZ KAZI: I believe we
have around 75 connectors that

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.610
connect to more than 400
data sources right now.

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:09.240
PETE FRISELLA: Sure.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.070
I mean, the data's the
most important part of it

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:11.730
to start with, right?

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:13.563
Without the data, you
can't do any analysis.

00:12:13.563 --> 00:12:15.949
So obviously, this is the
biggest component, right?

00:12:15.949 --> 00:12:17.490
Everybody has access
to lots of data.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:19.531
They're not necessarily
easy to get to sometimes,

00:12:19.531 --> 00:12:21.252
but this makes it much simpler.

00:12:21.252 --> 00:12:21.960
MINHAZ KAZI: Yep.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:23.376
And this gives you
the flexibility

00:12:23.376 --> 00:12:25.470
to have your
customized solution.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:28.500
You can bring in templates
that work with your community

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:31.290
connectors and provide you
with a very customized solution

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:35.010
either for your clients,
or for your customers,

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:37.780
or even for your
internal employees.

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.780
PETE FRISELLA: So we've
got the data, then next.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.930
MINHAZ KAZI: So
we have the data.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.180
Once you've brought your
data into Data Studio,

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.872
you can create some
nice visualizations.

00:12:46.872 --> 00:12:49.080
And we'll see how you can
build those visualizations.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.270
Let's say your visualization
is already built,

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:54.460
and now you want to share
your work with others.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.620
How can you do that?

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.220
There are multiple
ways available.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.053
The first is you can
just share with a link,

00:12:59.053 --> 00:13:03.480
just like Drive Documents.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:06.930
You can provide people with
view access or write access.

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:09.890
You can also embed
your Data Studio

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:13.890
report as a infographic or
a report in any web page,

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:15.420
or you can use it
as a presentation.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:19.030
We'll have a very quick look
at one of these examples.

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:21.450
This is a blog post
on the Cloud Big Data

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:24.660
blog where there was
analysis of the block chain

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:25.770
data for Bitcoin.

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:29.520
And over here, you can see there
are Data Studio dashboards that

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:31.179
are working on live data.

00:13:31.179 --> 00:13:32.970
And you can interact
with these dashboards.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.822
Right now, we can
pick a date range.

00:13:35.822 --> 00:13:36.780
Let's say we can pick--

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:38.460
PETE FRISELLA: So this is
on the Google Cloud blog,

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.392
