using Data Studio.

00:29:30.742 --> 00:29:31.950
This one is very interesting.

00:29:31.950 --> 00:29:37.770
This one shows log usage in
GCP, the Google Crowd Project--

00:29:37.770 --> 00:29:40.260
Google Cloud Platform--
where you can see usage

00:29:40.260 --> 00:29:41.670
of daily view, monthly view.

00:29:41.670 --> 00:29:44.100
And it's broken down
by different services.

00:29:44.100 --> 00:29:46.740
You can go into this,
you can figure the data.

00:29:46.740 --> 00:29:47.850
This is already created.

00:29:47.850 --> 00:29:49.850
And the good thing is you
can take this template

00:29:49.850 --> 00:29:51.240
and use it with
your own project.

00:29:51.240 --> 00:29:52.860
You don't have to create
this from scratch.

00:29:52.860 --> 00:29:55.120
That's one of the very nice
things about Data Studio

00:29:55.120 --> 00:29:57.450
is that anytime you
create something,

00:29:57.450 --> 00:29:59.970
you can let other people
take that template

00:29:59.970 --> 00:30:01.760
and build on top of your work.

00:30:01.760 --> 00:30:03.000
PETE FRISELLA: So you
can make a copy of this,

00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:04.620
and then connect to
your own data source,

00:30:04.620 --> 00:30:05.910
and it'll work
with your own data?

00:30:05.910 --> 00:30:06.360
MINHAZ KAZI: Exactly.

00:30:06.360 --> 00:30:07.590
PETE FRISELLA: Because
all the fields and things

00:30:07.590 --> 00:30:08.550
will be the same, yeah.

00:30:08.550 --> 00:30:12.930
MINHAZ KAZI: As long as
you're using a similar data

00:30:12.930 --> 00:30:15.540
set that has the same
field names and structure,

00:30:15.540 --> 00:30:18.530
your data should work.

00:30:18.530 --> 00:30:19.760
There's one other data set.

00:30:19.760 --> 00:30:23.980
This was made by Mark
Suarez, one of our partners.

00:30:23.980 --> 00:30:28.350
This is economical data
about US household income

00:30:28.350 --> 00:30:29.944
distribution by state.

00:30:29.944 --> 00:30:31.860
Over here, you can see
the income distribution

00:30:31.860 --> 00:30:34.110
for each different
state, sort of arranged

00:30:34.110 --> 00:30:36.990
in a geographic location-wise.

00:30:36.990 --> 00:30:39.660
You can see the income
distribution of the east side,

00:30:39.660 --> 00:30:42.990
west side, and sort of
very nice overall view that

00:30:42.990 --> 00:30:45.199
gives you a complete picture
of the whole community--

00:30:45.199 --> 00:30:47.031
PETE FRISELLA: Mark did
some nice work here.

00:30:47.031 --> 00:30:49.590
You have the representation of
the United States of America.

00:30:49.590 --> 00:30:50.910
And then individually,
you have these components

00:30:50.910 --> 00:30:52.860
that are showing income
distribution, right?

00:30:52.860 --> 00:30:53.735
MINHAZ KAZI: Exactly.

00:30:53.735 --> 00:30:55.950
PETE FRISELLA: So it's a
nice metaview of the country

00:30:55.950 --> 00:30:57.769
in that particular data set.

00:30:57.769 --> 00:30:58.560
MINHAZ KAZI: Right.

00:30:58.560 --> 00:30:59.810
PETE FRISELLA: It's very cool.

00:30:59.810 --> 00:31:01.560
MINHAZ KAZI: And let's
look at one more.

00:31:01.560 --> 00:31:03.330
This one came up
new, and this one

00:31:03.330 --> 00:31:07.230
shows a new feature that we
have that is pretty cool.

00:31:07.230 --> 00:31:10.267
This is data from the
Google Merchandise Store.

00:31:10.267 --> 00:31:11.600
This is bringing analytics data.

00:31:11.600 --> 00:31:14.800
The nice thing is it's
also pulling in the images.

00:31:14.800 --> 00:31:17.791
So if you have image
URLs in your data set,

00:31:17.791 --> 00:31:19.290
you can take that
image URL, and you

00:31:19.290 --> 00:31:22.410
can render the image in
your Data Studio dashboard.

00:31:22.410 --> 00:31:24.750
So for each item in
the analytics data,

00:31:24.750 --> 00:31:26.490
they're basically
pulling in that image

00:31:26.490 --> 00:31:28.680
and rendering it in
Data Studio to give

00:31:28.680 --> 00:31:31.210
a nice view of that product.

00:31:31.210 --> 00:31:34.020
PETE FRISELLA: So can we
see an example of that?

00:31:34.020 --> 00:31:37.860
Or we don't have
time right here?

00:31:37.860 --> 00:31:38.970
MINHAZ KAZI: Maybe--

00:31:38.970 --> 00:31:39.540
PETE FRISELLA: OK,
let's come back to it.

00:31:39.540 --> 00:31:39.900
MINHAZ KAZI: Yeah.

00:31:39.900 --> 00:31:42.270
The information's available
on our support site.

00:31:42.270 --> 00:31:44.890
You can see how
we can basically--

00:31:44.890 --> 00:31:46.890
any time you have an image
URL in your data set,

00:31:46.890 --> 00:31:47.945
you can just take that and--

00:31:47.945 --> 00:31:48.970
PETE FRISELLA: And
it'll render it.

00:31:48.970 --> 00:31:49.761
Yeah, that's great.

00:31:49.761 --> 00:31:52.080
MINHAZ KAZI: Exactly.

00:31:52.080 --> 00:31:54.630
And this one is a
very nice example

00:31:54.630 --> 00:32:02.130
where Data Studio was used to
showcase student information

00:32:02.130 --> 00:32:05.250
system data that has
school district metrics.

00:32:05.250 --> 00:32:08.550
You have days enrolled, how
many students were enrolled,

00:32:08.550 --> 00:32:11.610
different combination of
students, the race, the gender.

00:32:11.610 --> 00:32:15.840
And you can filter here to
pick up different grades.

00:32:15.840 --> 00:32:18.300
This is very helpful
for anyone who

00:32:18.300 --> 00:32:20.940
is sort of like an administrator
in a school system.

00:32:20.940 --> 00:32:26.256
And again, since this is a
general purpose dashboard,

00:32:26.256 --> 00:32:27.880
someone else who has
a similar data set

00:32:27.880 --> 00:32:30.752
can just use this-- copy it
and use it for their own uses.

00:32:30.752 --> 00:32:32.210
PETE FRISELLA: So
when you copy it,

00:32:32.210 --> 00:32:34.410
you can edit it and do anything
you want with every part

00:32:34.410 --> 00:32:34.900
itself, right?

00:32:34.900 --> 00:32:34.960
MINHAZ KAZI: Yes.

00:32:34.960 --> 00:32:35.800
PETE FRISELLA: You can
change things around,

00:32:35.800 --> 00:32:38.082
you can make adjustments,
change the data set.

00:32:38.082 --> 00:32:40.040
You can see how they
actually built the report.

00:32:40.040 --> 00:32:40.740
MINHAZ KAZI: Correct.

00:32:40.740 --> 00:32:41.410
PETE FRISELLA: It's
actually a great way

00:32:41.410 --> 00:32:43.870
to learn about how
to use the product.

00:32:43.870 --> 00:32:45.370
It's something that
we've definitely

00:32:45.370 --> 00:32:47.050
been trying to push people to
build more templates, really

00:32:47.050 --> 00:32:49.165
showcase what's possible
with their own data.

00:32:49.165 --> 00:32:51.040
And it's been working
really well for people.

00:32:51.040 --> 00:32:52.390
MINHAZ KAZI: Exactly.

00:32:52.390 --> 00:32:55.390
So these are the resources that
are available for Data Studio

00:32:55.390 --> 00:32:56.840
right now.

00:32:56.840 --> 00:32:58.885
We'd love for you to
